ety -76%), so there is no valuation cushion.","The fair-value models corroborate one another (dispersion 8%), and the Monte Carlo range runs $7.95 to $51.88 (P10-P90).","On multiples it looks expensive against Industrials peers: EV/EBITDA 17.2 vs 13.3 and P/FCF 39.8 vs 22.4 (sector median).","Against its own history it is dear: the EBIT multiple sits 16% above its 10-year median.","Earnings yields are thin: an FCF yield of 2.5% (below the risk-free rate) and an EBIT/EV of 3.9% (vs the 8% bar).","The 12 covering analysts target $52.17 on average, 54% above the price, well away from the model's fair value."],"prof":["ROIC of 10% earns above the cost of capital of 8.9%, but the 1pp spread is short of the 7pp moat bar; returns have swung a lot from year to year (CV 0.41).","It runs a 23% gross margin and converts 6% of revenue into free cash flow.","Earnings quality looks solid: a Piotroski score of 7/9 and cash conversion of 1.32x.","ROE of 10% comes mostly from margins and asset turnover rather than leverage (1.6x equity multiplier).","It spends 3.5% of revenue on R&D and 0.9% on stock compensation."],"hlth":["The balance sheet carries net cash of $300.0M (3% of market cap).","No distress or manipulation flags (Altman Z 3.7, in the safe zone)."],"growth":["Revenue has compounded at 10.6% over 3 years.","At current returns, reinvesting 33% of profits supports about 3.4% a year of fundamental growth, enough to sustain growth.","Forward indicators: a book-to-bill of 0.98, a backlog worth 2.3x annual revenue and deferred revenue up 47%.","Capex roughly matches depreciation (1.5x, 3.8% of sales), a maintenance pace.","It has beaten earnings estimates by 24.8% on average.","Analysts expect 2.5% long-term annual earnings growth."],"own":["Insiders own 71.5%, meaningful skin in the game, and institutions hold 28%.","Insiders have only sold over the past year (10 sales, net $4.5M sold).","Shareholder yield is a modest 1.4% (0.3% in buybacks and 1.1% in dividends)."],"people":[